## 2. Agent roles and responsibility boundaries

Each responsibility belongs to exactly one role. No role duplicates another's
mandate.

| Role | Owns (sole responsibility) | Produces | Must not |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Strategic Orchestrator** | Intent → decomposition, model routing, budget allocation, conflict resolution, final accept/reject | Task Packets (§7), decision log | Write manifests |
| **Engineering Orchestrator** | Turning a Task Packet into merged, tested code | Diffs, specs, `regent` runs, status report | Redefine scope or accept its own work |
| **Architect** | Class/defined-type structure, parameter contracts, data layout, Hiera strategy | Design notes, parameter stubs | Implement beyond stubs |
| **Backend Engineer** | `manifests/`, `lib/puppet/` functions, facts, types, providers | Puppet + Ruby source with specs | Touch CI or packaging |
| **Frontend Engineer** | `templates/`, rendered config, README and reference docs, user-facing output | ERB/EPP + docs | Change resource logic |
| **DevOps Engineer** | `metadata.json`, dependencies, OS support, CI workflows, release/publish | Metadata + pipeline changes | Change module behaviour |
| **Security Engineer** | Secret handling, `Sensitive` usage, file modes, privilege boundaries, dependency audit | Findings with severity + fix | Ship functional features |
| **Research Agent** | Fact-finding across this module, its dependencies, and upstream docs | ≤2 000-token brief with citations | Make the decision |
| **Reviewer Agent** | Correctness, idempotence, regression risk, invariant (§0) compliance | Verdict + ranked findings | Edit the code it reviews |
| **Simulation Agent** | Forecasting: rollout blast radius, node impact, convergence risk, cost | Scenario table + confidence | Assert facts it did not simulate |

**Boundary rules**

1. A role that needs work outside its column raises a *handoff*; it does not
   widen its own scope.
2. The Reviewer Agent is never the instance that produced the artifact.
3. Only the Strategic Orchestrator discusses scope with the human; only the
   Engineering Orchestrator reports test status.

**Seat and family.** Each role reports to exactly one orchestrator, and that
decides which model family it runs on.

| Seat | Roles | Family |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Strategic Orchestrator (Claude) | Architect, Research Agent, Reviewer Agent | Claude Sonnet / Claude Opus |
| Engineering Orchestrator (Codex) | Backend, Frontend, DevOps, Security, Simulation Agent | GPT-6 Mini / GPT-6 / GPT Terra / GPT Sol |

The Simulation Agent runs on GPT Sol and the long-context reader on GPT Terra, so
both sit in the engineering seat. Claude interprets their output; it does not run
them.


